## Summary

**Changed:** `/tmp/epam-bench-epam-ts-003-wjYygO/src/queue.ts`

**Fix Applied:** 
- Replaced `this.items.pop()` with `this.items.shift()` in the `drain()` method

**Why:** 
- `pop()` removes from the end of an array (LIFO - Last In, First Out)
- `shift()` removes from the beginning of an array (FIFO - First In, First Out)

**Verification Results:**
- ✅ All 4 tests pass including "drain returns items in FIFO order"
- ✅ Test files remain unmodified
- ✅ TypeScript compiles without errors in source code (`tsc --noEmit --skipLibCheck`)

The Queue class now correctly implements standard queue semantics, returning items in the order they were enqueued rather than in reverse order.

